// What a file may not name. `private` is what a declaration says when it
// says nothing, so each of these is refused for a different reason: the
// helper is nobody else's business, the package one is the group's own, and
// a modifier where no declaration follows is not a modifier at all.

import "./visibility-lib/hidden.keal"

println(open())
println(secret())
println(shared())
val t: Kept = Kept(1)
println(t.n)

// Members, too. A class keeps its own counsel — a member that says nothing
// is private — while a record IS its fields, so theirs follow the record.
val c = Counter(1)
c.bump()
println(c.n)
println(c.secret)
c.hidden()
c.secret = 3
val p = Marker(1, 2)
println(p.x)
println(p.hidden)
